// Filename:	MLPRO 2 TOF Interface PCB.test
// Project:		MLPRO 2
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    06.03.2024 Rev1
//
// Description: Tests the MLPRO 2  TOF PCB
// 
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.

#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box above.
c. Using SW1 on the PCB set the address to position 5. 
COMMENT: *Example image below*
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
DISPLAY: TOFSetAddress.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#2: Setup equipment 1
a. Set adjustable PSU output 1 to 12V ±0.1V, 1.5A ±0.1A and switch the output off.
b. Using TE159, connect the PSU to the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
d. Connect the USB cable from the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086) to the PC. 
COMMENT: *Example image below*
DISPLAY: TE192Setup.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#3: Setup equipment 2
a. Connect the PCB (PL2) to the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).   
b. Connect cable A to X2 on the PCB.
c. Connect cable B to X1 on the PCB.
d. Connect the flat flex cable to j2 on the PCB
e. Fit the PCB to the ML PRO PCB Fixture 1 (TE190) can connect the test PCB (TE068).
f. Switch the output of the adjustable PSU on and power on the MLPRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
IMPORTANT: Ensure the blue paper is covering the LED window before powering on.
DISPLAY: TOF Setup.jpg
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: MLPRO2 
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #2

#4: PCB communication check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  BENUM
READLINE: MLPRO2  BENUM
IF:
Check the expected result is a match with the Returned result.
Expected result is = RS2

Returned result is = %BENUM%
ELSE:
Bad result . . . sorry
PASS_FAIL: #4


#5: LED off test
View the LED window and check that the LED is off.
DISPLAY: TOF LED.png
PASS_FAIL: #5

#6: Ringlight driver test
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 001111 1023
Check the Red LED is on.
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: MLPRO2  READAMPS 
READLINE: MLPRO2  READAMPS
The returned Current is = %READAMPS%

RANGE: %READAMPS% 372 30					// PASS if value is between a range
IF:											// IF a ture result the next line below actions
GOTO: #6.1: 								// if results match goto next test
IMPORTANT: This test has failed 
Unexpected current reading 					// print this for test log information
PASS_FAIL: #6 								// Increments fail count and adds comment in log file
GOTO: #7


#6.1: Ringlight driver test - test passed
TEST: PASSED
Result = Test Pass
CLICK_OK:								// Increments PASS count and adds comment in log file
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 000000 0


#7: Focus LED test
IMPORTANT: Ensure the blue paper is covering the LED window before powering on.
CLICK_OK:
COMMAND: MLPRO2 RING 000000 0
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FOCUSLED 1
a. Check the Red LED is on.
PASS_FAIL: #7
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FOCUSLED 0


#8: Range finder test
COMMAND: MLPRO2  RRB
READLINE: MLPRO2  RRB
The returned Range finder distance is = %RRB%

RANGE: %RRB% 60 5							// PASS if value is between a range
IF:											// IF a ture result the next line below actions
GOTO: #8.1: 								// if results match goto next test
IMPORTANT: This test has failed 
Unexpected reading 							// print this for test log information
PASS_FAIL: #8								// Increments fail count and adds comment in log file
GOTO: #9


#8.1: Range finder test - test passed
TEST: PASSED
Result = Test Pass
CLICK_OK:									// Increments PASS count and adds comment in log file


#9: Test complete:
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#							// turn off any LEDs still on 
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and then power off the PSU and disconnect the PCB.
CLICK_OK:


#QUIT:
DISCONNECT: MLPRO2
// End of file
